WHAT THIS DATA IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT

`results/mos/` contains anonymous listening-study data: per-pair mean opinion
scores, per-session response records under a random session code, and the
derived analysis outputs. No personal data was collected at any point. The
survey was configured with response anonymisation enabled, so no IP address,
location, or contact detail exists in any file here, and this was verified
against the released exports rather than assumed.

The study was reviewed and approved by the UCL Computer Science Low Risk Ethics
Committee (Project ID 4972). The approved application provides for the
anonymous ratings and the aggregated per-clip averages to be deposited in a
repository and shared alongside a publication, which is what this release does.

The generated audio stimuli are NOT included and may not be redistributed. The
approved application states that the AI-generated segments are used only as
private research stimuli. The perturbation battery is instead rebuilt from its
sources by the released scripts; see README.md.
